Subject: [PATCH] Store all user files in internal storage only

fluddokt.opsu.fake.File is the abstraction every core path goes through, and
its constructor preferred Gdx.files.external(...) on any non-desktop platform.
libGDX maps external to Environment.getExternalStorageDirectory() on Android,
so beatmaps, skins, replays, screenshots, opsu.cfg and opsu.log all landed on
shared storage and needed runtime permissions.

Gdx.files.local maps to Context.getFilesDir() on Android and to the working
directory on desktop, so switching to local satisfies the internal-storage
requirement on mobile without breaking the desktop or iOS builds.

Absolute paths are still honoured when they already exist, because opsu.cfg
persists absolute directory paths (BeatmapDirectory and friends) that older
external-storage builds wrote. StorageMigration clears those, but they must
not break before migration runs.
